[32m+[m[32m## 3. Key Architectural Decisions Log[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Modular Monolith for Backend:** Selected to eliminate microservice operational overhead while enforcing clean domain separation via package boundaries. (See [ADR-001](docs/architecture/adr/ADR-001-MODULAR-MONOLITH.md)).[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **PostgreSQL 16 + PostGIS 3.4:** Primary datastore for spatial drainage line networks, catch basins, and spatial queries (`ST_DWithin`, `ST_Contains`).[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Offline-First Android App:** SQLite/Room encrypted queue storing observations locally until network connectivity is confirmed, ensuring zero field data loss.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **SHA-256 Media Hashing:** Cryptographic hashing performed client-side upon capture to guarantee evidence immutability and anti-tampering.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 4. Known Issues & Technical Risks[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Risk 1 — Field GPS Accuracy:** GPS drift under urban canopy or near tall structures may mislocate drainage assets. *Mitigation:* Require manual map-pin verification and capture heading/bearing metadata.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Risk 2 — Heavy Media Sync Overhead:** High-resolution videos/photos captured in low-connectivity areas may stall sync queues. *Mitigation:* Background chunked uploading, adaptive compression, and prioritization of metadata JSON before media binaries.[m
[32m+[m
